1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Sol Zero separates scientific reasoning from the world implementation

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Omnigent agents call Python function tools through a fixed public HTTP
interface

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Generator code and admin scores remain outside the agents'
environment.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Each specialist owns a decision and returns structured records

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Theorist laws feed candidate selection

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Pre registered predictions feed the Operator

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Measurements feed Analyst verdicts

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The principal investigator owns the stopping decision and final
mission.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,750
Shared Pydantic records connect client and server

10
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:37,500
Prediction tables must cover every live law before execution

11
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,250
The server enforces the twelve experiment budget, including failed
measurements

12
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:45,000
Insufficient evidence remains a valid scientific verdict.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The durable ledger captures laws, candidates, predictions, results,
verdicts, nominations, decision changes, and commitment

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
This run records six changed plans

15
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Reviewers can inspect the evidence behind the decisions, rather than
trusting a summary.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,750
Tool policies restrict robot access, check safe settings, and gate
commitment

17
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:07,500
Development uses explicit automatic approval; interactive demos
default to human approval

18
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:11,250
Checkpoints preserve progress

19
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:15,000
Ambiguous experiment responses fail closed instead of being blindly
replayed.

20
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,750
Provider limits exposed substantial overhead

21
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:22,500
Current code adds exponential backoff with jitter, compact structured
context, and at most three candidates

22
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,250
The Operator now executes without a model turn

23
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:30,000
End to end savings still need measurement.

24
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
The preserved baseline used the earlier Operator implementation

25
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Its investigator stopped after ten experiments, and the server graded
five mission hits

26
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The repository includes its ledger, score, measurement notes, and
evidence hashes for independent inspection.

27
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
This is a compressed replay of a development simulation, not a
physical robot or held out validation

28
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The run took seventeen active minutes

29
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The next test compares laboratory, random, and single agent conditions
with shared tools and budgets.
